EVIDENCE: Most megaslides of these MTCs are siliciclastic in nature, sourced from sea-bed deformations generated by multistage rotation or the sliding of large upslope blocks (from 30 to 60 km wide). Blocks deformation was triggered by fluid overpressure along a regional Upper Miocene condensed section, horizon H3, which also acts as the regional décollement level for gravity tectonics in the basin;
REASONING: The source text indicates that the deformation of large upslope blocks is triggered by fluid overpressure, which can be inferred to initiate or trigger megaslides.
VERDICT: WEAK_SUPPORT
